  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-25T20:08:06.412Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In one of the recent updates, a change was made so that players would only appear in a world after around 30 seconds after the world loaded. This dramatically increased performance for me on populated worlds. Before, if I spawned in and a bunch of people were in front of me I would permanently get extremely low framerates. I used to have to look up in an extremely tall avatar when loading in so that I wouldn't get the framerate issue. The delayed player loading completely fixed the isue for me. However, as of the latest update players load in instantly again, so I'm getting extremely low framerates if I load into a world normally. I'm not sure if this was intentional or not, but please at least add an option to turn on delayed player loading.",
